patrone-gnome-taskbar (0.1.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hide GNOME's screen-sharing indicator in desktops with no screen of
    their own (Patrone's): there it's always on, for the very Remote Desktop
    connection the desktop is seen through, and any click on it, a
    right-click included, cut that connection. It showed as two unexplained
    icons in the tray.
  * Style the screen-sharing and screen-recording indicators for the tray
    (an orange or red pill with white icons), where they still show.
  * Keep the tray from ever expanding: GNOME's top bar buttons ask to.

